      },
      "message": "fix(motion): a plain two-ring bar fits its true axis and wraps; the seam refusal names its causes\n\nA bar meshed as two rings (long side facets, axis-fan caps - how CAD\nexports a cylinder) was refused by the rotary wrap as \"a feature that\nis not turned crosses the seam\". The cause was the axis fit: every side\nfacet anchors its normal line at the bar's mid-station, so no line sees\na tilt about it. The eigen direction was exact, but the refinement\nreturned a 26-microradian tilt and the fit kept it on a residual lower\nby rounding noise. The leaning axis put the cap centres a micron off it\nat arbitrary azimuths, and their facets read as 15 to 38 seam columns.\n\n- axis_refine::worth_refining: an eigen line already concurrent to\n  rounding (residual under 1e-9 mm per mm of radius) is not refined.\n- rotary_seam: seam columns are grouped at the weld grid's grain\n  (1e-6 rad, was 1e-9), still far finer than any flat's ragged seam.\n- The seam refusal also names a mesh whose diameters were tessellated\n  with different column counts, and says what to do about each cause.\n\nFixes #228\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
